## Algorithms and test samples

The workload and test generator use two published random-number algorithms:

- SplitMix64 initialization by Sebastiano Vigna (2015).
- The xoroshiro128+ transition by David Blackman and Sebastiano Vigna (2016; parameters 55/14/36).

Their authors dedicate the reference implementations to the public domain and permit use, copying, modification and distribution:

- https://prng.di.unimi.it/splitmix64.c
- https://prng.di.unimi.it/xoroshiro128plus.c

`tests/itch_test.cpp` identifies retained public Nasdaq sample records used for decoder cases. The demonstration and hand-written lifecycle ledgers are original fixtures.

